IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc27-s737-1-restitution`

-- ccc27-tests-s737-1.l4 -- tests for sections 737.1 to 741.2. Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.

§ `Tests -- sections 737.1 to 741.2`

-- 737.1(1)
#ASSERT `s 737.1(1) the court shall consider making a restitution order under section 738 or 739` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- convicted
#ASSERT `s 737.1(1) the court shall consider making a restitution order under section 738 or 739` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- discharged under section 730
#ASSERT `s 737.1(1) the court shall consider making a restitution order under section 738 or 739` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither: "If an offender is convicted or is discharged"

-- 737.1(2)
#ASSERT `s 737.1(2) the court shall inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to give the victims an opportunity to indicate whether they are seeking restitution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(2) the court shall inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to give the victims an opportunity to indicate whether they are seeking restitution` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before a finding of guilt
#ASSERT `s 737.1(2) the court has made the inquiry before imposing the sentence` (Date 9 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 737.1(2) the court has made the inquiry before imposing the sentence` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the same day: a date does not say which came first
#ASSERT `s 737.1(2) the court has made the inquiry before imposing the sentence` (Date 11 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the sentence

-- 737.1(3): "On application of the prosecutor or on its own motion ... if the court is satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 737.1(3) the court may adjourn the proceedings to permit the victims to indicate whether they are seeking restitution or to establish their losses and damages` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(3) the court may adjourn the proceedings to permit the victims to indicate whether they are seeking restitution or to establish their losses and damages` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied: F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(3) the court may adjourn the proceedings to permit the victims to indicate whether they are seeking restitution or to establish their losses and damages` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither an application of the prosecutor nor the court's own motion (an "on" gate, ruling (b))

-- 737.1(4)
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by the method` `s 737.1(4) completing Form 34.1 in Part XXVIII` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by the method` `s 737.1(4) completing a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by the method` `s 737.1(4) using another method approved by the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by the method` `s 737.1(4) using a method that none of those approves` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the individual indicates on the victim's behalf, by s 2.2` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the answer of section 2.2 is passed on
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the individual indicates on the victim's behalf, by s 2.2` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the individual indicates on the victim's behalf, by s 2.2` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- NOTHING stays NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the person seeking restitution has met the requirement to establish readily ascertainable losses and damages` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the person seeking restitution has met the requirement to establish readily ascertainable losses and damages` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- amount not readily ascertainable
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the person seeking restitution has met the requirement to establish readily ascertainable losses and damages` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not established in the same manner
#ASSERT `s 737.1(4) the person seeking restitution has met the requirement to establish readily ascertainable losses and damages` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not seeking restitution: the requirement does not arise

-- 737.1(5)
#ASSERT `s 737.1(5) the court shall include in the record a statement of its reasons for not making a restitution order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 737.1(5) the court shall include in the record a statement of its reasons for not making a restitution order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court made an order
#ASSERT `s 737.1(5) the court shall include in the record a statement of its reasons for not making a restitution order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no victim sought restitution

-- 738(1)
#ASSERT `s 738(1) the court may order the offender to make restitution to another person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 738(1) the court may order the offender to make restitution to another person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- discharged under section 730
#ASSERT `s 738(1) the court may order the offender to make restitution to another person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither convicted nor discharged ("Where", ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 738(1) the court may order the offender to make restitution to another person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not on application of the Attorney General nor on the court's own motion ("on", ruling (b))
-- 738(1)(a): replacement value less the value of any part returned
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` TRUE 1000 300 TRUE EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` TRUE 1000 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST 1000   -- nothing returned
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` TRUE 1000 1000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 0   -- all of it returned
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` TRUE 1000 300 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not readily ascertainable
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` FALSE 1000 300 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a result of the offence or the arrest
-- 738(1)(b): all pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(b) the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm` TRUE 2500 TRUE EQUALS JUST 2500
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(b) the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm` TRUE 2500 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(b) the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm` FALSE 2500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 738(1)(c): the actual and reasonable expenses of moving out of the household
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(c) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of the offender's household` TRUE TRUE 800 TRUE EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(c) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of the offender's household` TRUE FALSE 800 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a member of the household
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(c) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of the offender's household` TRUE TRUE 800 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(c) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of the offender's household` FALSE TRUE 800 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 738(1)(d): an offence under section 402.2 or 403
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(d) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` (`Provision of the Code` OF 402.2, "(1)") TRUE 450 TRUE EQUALS JUST 450
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(d) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` (`Provision of the Code` OF 403, "(1)") TRUE 450 TRUE EQUALS JUST 450
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(d) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` (`Provision of the Code` OF 404, "") TRUE 450 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not section 402.2 or 403
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(d) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` (`Provision of the Code` OF 403, "(1)") TRUE 450 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 738(1)(e): an offence under subsection 162.1(1)
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(e) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing the intimate image` (`Provision of the Code` OF 162.1, "(1)") TRUE 120 TRUE EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(e) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing the intimate image` (`Provision of the Code` OF 162.1, "(2)") TRUE 120 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- subsection 162.1(2) is not named
#ASSERT `s 738(1)(e) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing the intimate image` (`Provision of the Code` OF 162.1, "(1)") TRUE 120 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 739
#ASSERT `s 739 the court may order the offender to pay restitution to the person` TRUE FALSE `s 739(a) a person to whom property obtained by the offence was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, acting in good faith and without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 739 the court may order the offender to pay restitution to the person` FALSE TRUE `s 739(b) a person from whom the offender borrowed money on the security of that property, acting in good faith and without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- discharged; head (b)
#ASSERT `s 739 the court may order the offender to pay restitution to the person` TRUE FALSE `s 739(a) a person to whom property obtained by the offence was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, acting in good faith and without notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the property has not been returned ("where", ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 739 the court may order the offender to pay restitution to the person` FALSE FALSE `s 739(a) a person to whom property obtained by the offence was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, acting in good faith and without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither convicted nor discharged
#ASSERT `s 739 the ceiling on restitution to the person` `s 739(a) a person to whom property obtained by the offence was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, acting in good faith and without notice` 5000 3000 EQUALS 5000   -- the amount of consideration
#ASSERT `s 739 the ceiling on restitution to the person` `s 739(b) a person from whom the offender borrowed money on the security of that property, acting in good faith and without notice` 5000 3000 EQUALS 3000   -- the total amount outstanding in respect of the loan

-- 739.1
#ASSERT `s 739.1 the offender's financial means or ability to pay prevents the court from making an order under section 738 or 739` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not prevent"
#ASSERT `s 739.1 the offender's financial means or ability to pay prevents the court from making an order under section 738 or 739` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- some other ground: the section is silent

-- 739.2
#ASSERT `s 739.2 the term of payment the court shall require in the order` FALSE EQUALS `s 739.2 payment of the full amount specified in the order by the day specified in the order`
#ASSERT `s 739.2 the term of payment the court shall require in the order` TRUE EQUALS `s 739.2 payment in instalments under a periodic payment scheme set out in the order`

-- 739.3
#ASSERT `s 739.3 the order must specify the amount that is payable to each person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 739.3 the order must specify the amount that is payable to each person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in which case": only where there is more than one person
#ASSERT `s 739.3 the order may specify the order of priority in which those persons are to be paid` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 739.3 the order may specify the order of priority in which those persons are to be paid` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "those persons": one person is not covered

-- 739.4(1)
#ASSERT `s 739.4(1) the court may make the order in favour of a public authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 739.4(1) the court may make the order in favour of a public authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the body is not a designated public authority: who is designated is outside the sources
#ASSERT `s 739.4(1) the court may make the order in favour of a public authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no request ("On the request", ruling (b))

-- 740
#ASSERT `s 740 the court shall first make the order of restitution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb (a): a forfeiture order may be made in respect of the same property
#ASSERT `s 740 the court shall first make the order of restitution` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb (b): the offender could not comply with both a restitution order and a fine
#ASSERT `s 740 the court shall first make the order of restitution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither limb
#ASSERT `s 740 the court shall first make the order of restitution` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court does not find a restitution order applicable and appropriate

-- 740.1
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the portion of the order that relates to the requirement for payment is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739` `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 732.1` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the portion of the order that relates to the requirement for payment is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739` `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 742.3` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the portion of the order that relates to the requirement for payment is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739` `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 742.3` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the order has not terminated early
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the portion of the order that relates to the requirement for payment is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739` `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 732.1` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no requirement for payment
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the portion of the order that relates to the requirement for payment is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739` `s 740.1 an order of another kind` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the restitution order remains in force` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- payments outstanding
#ASSERT `s 740.1 the restitution order remains in force` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until all the required payments are made"

-- 741(1)
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `s 741(1) an order under section 738` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `s 741(1) an order under section 742.3` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a missed periodic payment
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `s 741(1) an order under section 739` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- paid in full and on time
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `s 741(1) an order under section 732.1` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `s 741(1) an order of another kind` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in default: F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the order is not filed
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a court without jurisdiction to enter the judgment
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the judgment is enforceable against the offender as if it were a judgment rendered against the offender in civil proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741(1) the judgment is enforceable against the offender as if it were a judgment rendered against the offender in civil proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 741(2)
#ASSERT `s 741(2) all or any part of the amount may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741(2) all or any part of the amount may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court has not so directed
#ASSERT `s 741(2) all or any part of the amount may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- ownership is disputed by other claimants
#ASSERT `s 741(2) all or any part of the amount may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not moneys found on the offender at the arrest
#ASSERT `s 741(2) all or any part of the amount may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an amount under section 738 or 739

-- 741.1
#ASSERT `s 741.1 the court shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the recipient` `s 741.1 the person to whom the restitution is ordered to be paid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741.1 the court shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the recipient` `s 741.1 the public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741.1 the court shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the recipient` `s 741.1 the person to whom the public authority is to remit amounts received under the order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 741.1 the court shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the recipient` `s 741.1 the public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- paid to the person direct: no public authority to notify
#ASSERT `s 741.1 the court shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the recipient` `s 741.1 the person to whom the restitution is ordered to be paid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no order of restitution

-- 741.2
#ASSERT `s 741.2 a civil remedy for an act or omission is affected by the restitution order` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not affected by reason only"
#ASSERT `s 741.2 a civil remedy for an act or omission is affected by the restitution order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another reason: the section is silent
